    "description": "A warehouse with its inbound lane. Containers dispatched to it travel through three in-transit stages (an Erlang-3 lead time, so transit times spread out realistically and every container in transit is counted) before reaching on-hand stock; the lane is expedited while stock is below a threshold. It forecasts demand by exponential smoothing and sets its order rate by an order-up-to rule: order the forecast plus a correction towards forecast x (lead time + stock cover), but only while the inventory position (on hand plus in transit) is below target. Lead times are per warehouse; stock cover, adjustment and smoothing times are shared by every warehouse in the model.",
